      "id": 1,
      "text": "Royal Center was platted in April 1846 by Elisee Andrews as a speculative venture on 41 lots in Boone Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_center_indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Logansport & Chicago Railroad arrived around 1860, turning Royal Center into a bustling lumber and grain shipping hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_center_indiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Carnegie library built in the early 1900s sits at 203 North Chicago Street, a historic architectural gem in town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_center_indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Royal Center’s name supposedly comes from a town in New York, reflecting early settlers’ origins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Center%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Situated in the Wabash River basin, the area faces occasional flooding from the river and heavy seasonal rains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_center_indiana",
